\nTitle: Statistics on parallelogram polyominoes and a q,t-analogue of the Narayana numbers\nAuthors: Jean-Christophe Aval, Michele D'Adderio, Mark Dukes, Angela Hicks, Yvan Le Borgne\nDate: Mon Jan 21 10:23:10 2013\n\nWe study the statistics area, bounce and dinv on the set of parallelogram polyominoes having a rectangular m times n bounding box. We show that the bi-statistics (area, bounce) and (area, dinv) give rise to the same q,t-analogue of Narayana numbers which was introduced by two of the authors in [arXiv:1208.0024]. We prove the main conjectures of that paper: the q,t-Narayana polynomials are symmetric in both q and t, and m and n. This is accomplished by providing a symmetric functions interpretation of the q,t-Narayana polynomials which relates them to the famous diagonal harmonics.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYet another doubly refined enumeration of Alternating Sign... (https://arxivlens.com/paperview/details/yet-another-doubly-refined-enumeration-of-alternating-sign-matrices-8008-eda8e712)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Crawled: last month; Guo-Niu Han, Lihong Yang ... Since the alternating sign matrix conjecture, proposed by Mills, Robbins, and Rumsey in 1982, was proved by Zeilberger and Kuperberg, several refined enumerations have been considered. ... We present a refinement of that decomposition conjecture.\n\nBack ArXiv math.CO Yet another doubly refined enumeration of Alternating Sign Matrices\n\nArXiv math.CO\n\n# Yet another doubly refined enumeration of Alternating Sign Matrices\n\nGuo-Niu Han, Lihong Yang\n\n2601.10870 Published Jan 15, 2026\n\nChat with paper Cite 中文 View PDF Share\n\n### Publication\n\nPublished: Jan 15, 2026\n\nCategories: math.CO\n\n### Metrics\n\nSource: ArXiv\n\n### Paper Preview\n\n### Abstract\n\nSince the alternating sign matrix conjecture, proposed by Mills, Robbins, and Rumsey in 1982, was proved by Zeilberger and Kuperberg, several refined enumerations have been considered. In particular, Behrend et al. obtained a quadruply refined enumeration by adding certain parameters. In this paper, we revisit the doubly refined enumeration of alternating sign matrices by adding three parameters: the number of $-1$'s, the position of the $1$ in the first row, and the position of the $1$ in the last row. Using Lascoux's formula on symmetry functions, we derive a new determinantal formula for this doubly refined enumeration. Besides the enumeration conjecture, Mills et al. also proposed a decomposition conjecture, which was subsequently proven by Kuperberg. We present a refinement of that decomposition conjecture.\n\n### Paper Details\n\nPaper ID: 2601.10870\n\nComments: 19 pages\n\nCategories:\n\nmath.CO\n\nView on arXiv Download PDF\n\n### How to Cite This Paper\n\n[Button: BibTeX] [Button: APA] [Button: MLA] [Button: Chicago] [Button: IEEE]\n\nReference manager: RIS EndNote\n\n### Authors\n\nGN Guo-Niu Han 7 papers LY Lihong Yang 70 papers--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nParallelogram polyominoes, partially labelled Dyck paths, and the Delta conjecture (FULL VERSION) (https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.08787)\nciteturn2academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.9 years ago; We introduce area, bounce and dinv statistics on decorated parallelogram polyominoes, and prove that some of their q,t-enumerators match $\\langle \\Delta_{h_m} e_{n+1},s_{k+1,1^{n-k}}\\rangle$, extending in this way the work in (Aval et al. ... This is the full version of (D'Adderio, Iraci 2017) arXiv:1711.03923.\nTitle: Parallelogram polyominoes, partially labelled Dyck paths, and the Delta conjecture (FULL VERSION)\nAuthors: Michele D'Adderio, Alessandro Iraci\nDate: Sat Dec 23 15:08:50 2017\n\nWe introduce area, bounce and dinv statistics on decorated parallelogram polyominoes, and prove that some of their q,t-enumerators match $\\langle \\Delta_{h_m} e_{n+1},s_{k+1,1^{n-k}}\\rangle$, extending in this way the work in (Aval et al. 2014). Also, we provide a bijective connection between decorated parallelogram polyominoes and decorated labelled Dyck paths, which allows us to prove the combinatorial interpretation of the coefficient $\\langle \\Delta_{e_{m+n-k-1}}'e_{m+n},h_m h_n\\rangle$ predicted by the Delta conjecture in (Haglund et al. 2015). Finally, we define a statistic pmaj on partially labelled Dyck paths, which provides another conjectural combinatorial interpretation of $\\Delta_{h_{\\ell}}\\Delta_{e_{n-k-1}}'e_n$, cf. (Haglund et al. 2015). This is the full version of (D'Adderio, Iraci 2017) arXiv:1711.03923.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStatistics on parallelogram polyominoes and a q,t-analogue of the Narayana numbers - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/1301.4803v1)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.8 years ago; Crawled: last week; We study the statistics area, bounce and dinv on the set of parallelogram polyominoes having a rectangular m times n bounding box. We show that the bi-statistics (area, bounce) and (area, dinv) give rise to the same q,t-analogue of Narayana numbers which was introduced by two of the authors in [arXiv:1208.0024].\n\n## Statistics on parallelogram polyominoes and a q,t-analogue of the Narayana numbers\n\nJean-Christophe Aval, Michele D'Adderio, Mark Dukes, Angela Hicks, Yvan Le Borgne\n\nPublished: 2013-01-21\n\nDOI: 10.1016/j.jcta.2013.09.001\n\ndinv narayana number parallelogram polyomino polyomino symmetric function polynomial\n\n### Abstract\n\nWe study the statistics area, bounce and dinv on the set of parallelogram polyominoes having a rectangular m times n bounding box. We show that the bi-statistics (area, bounce) and (area, dinv) give rise to the same q,t-analogue of Narayana numbers which was introduced by two of the authors in [arXiv:1208.0024]. We prove the main conjectures of that paper: the q,t-Narayana polynomials are symmetric in both q and t, and m and n. This is accomplished by providing a symmetric functions interpretation of the q,t-Narayana polynomials which relates them to the famous diagonal harmonics.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStatistics on parallelogram polyominoes and a (https://www.labri.fr/perso/aval/ADDHL-long.pdf)\nciteturn2search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; parallelogram polyominoes having a rectangular m × n bounding box. ... two statistics on these combinatorial objects, area and bounce, which led to\n1. Introduction\nA parallelogram polyomino having an m × n bounding box is a polyomino\nin a rectangle consisting of m × n cells that is formed by cutting out two\n(possibly empty) non-touching standard Young tableaux which have corners\nat (0, n) and (m, 0).\nAn example of a parallelogram polyomino having a\n12 × 7 bounding box is illustrated in Figure 1. Let Polyom,n be the set of all\nparallelogram polyominoes having a rectangular m × n bounding box. The\ncardinality of Polyom,n is known to be N(m + n −1, m) where for positive\nintegers a and b,\n\u0013\nN(a, b) := 1\na\n\u0012a\nb\n\u0013\u0012\na\nb −1\nare the famous Narayana numbers. Two authors of this work introduced [4]\ntwo statistics on these combinatorial objects, area and bounce, which led to\na q, t-analogue of the Narayana numbers N(m + n −1, m), namely\nNaram,n(q, t) :=\nX\nP∈Polyom,n\nqarea(P)tbounce(P),\nthat they called the q, t-Narayana polynomial. In that same work it was\nconjectured that the q, t-Narayana polynomials are symmetric in q and t,\nand as expressions were also symmetric in m and n. We introduce a new\nstatistic dinv which gives a new q, t-analogue of the same numbers\ng\nNaram,n(q, t) :=\nX\nP\nqdinv(P)tarea(P).\nThe following theorem establishes a relation between these two polyno-\nmials.\nTheorem 4.1. For all m ≥1 and n ≥1, we have\nNaram,n(q, t) = g\nNaran,m(q, t).\nWe give two proofs of this result, one using an explicit bijection, and\nanother one using a recursion. The main result of this paper is the proof of\nthe symmetries conjectured in [4].\nTheorem 6.2. For all m ≥1 and n ≥1, we have\nNaram,n(q, t) = Naram,n(t, q)\n2--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nParallelogram polyominoes, partially labelled Dyck paths, and the Delta conjecture (https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.03923)\nciteturn2academia16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.0 years ago; We introduce area, bounce and dinv statistics on decorated parallelogram polyominoes, and prove that some of their q,t-enumerators match $\\langle \\Delta_{h_m} e_{n+1}, s_{k+1,1^{n-k}} \\rangle$, extending in this way the work in (Aval et al.\nTitle: Parallelogram polyominoes, partially labelled Dyck paths, and the Delta conjecture\nAuthors: Michele D'Adderio, Alessandro Iraci\nDate: Fri Nov 10 17:13:19 2017\n\nWe introduce area, bounce and dinv statistics on decorated parallelogram polyominoes, and prove that some of their q,t-enumerators match $\\langle \\Delta_{h_m} e_{n+1}, s_{k+1,1^{n-k}} \\rangle$, extending in this way the work in (Aval et al. 2014). Also, we provide a bijective connection between decorated parallelogram polyominoes and decorated labelled Dyck paths, which allows us to prove the combinatorial interpretation of the coefficient $\\langle\\Delta_{e_{m+n-k-1}}'e_{m+n}, h_m h_n \\rangle$ predicted by the Delta conjecture in (Haglund et al. 2015). Finally, we define a statistic pmaj on partially labelled Dyck paths, which provides another conjectural combinatorial interpretation of $\\Delta_{h_{\\ell}}\\Delta_{e_{n-k-1}}'e_n$, cf. (Haglund et al. 2015). This is an extended abstract of (D'Adderio, Iraci 2017): this forthcoming publication will have proofs and additional details and results.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nParallelogram polyominoes, partially labelled Dyck paths, and the Delta conject